WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:09.751
The bumblebee reappeared.

2
00:00:10.611 --> 00:00:18.496
She was at the edge of a forest by a suburban backyard.

3
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.003
A girl named Daisy Lewis was in that backyard.

4
00:00:35.023 --> 00:00:38.987
So was her best friend, Kaleem Carter, who lived next door.

5
00:00:39.807 --> 00:00:43.150
They were sprawled on the grass, painting cardboard signs.

6
00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:46.933
"Hand me the purple glitter paint, please," Daisy said.

7
00:00:46.953 --> 00:00:51.036
"I want our names to really pop!"

8
00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:00.024
The friends were making signs to advertise their pet-sitting and dog-walking business.

9
00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:02.913
Daisy was only ten years old.

10
00:01:05.454 --> 00:01:09.336
But everyone said she was very responsible and had a way with animals.

11
00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:13.897
She couldn't have a pet of her own because of her dad's asthma.

12
00:01:14.618 --> 00:01:17.299
But she loved taking care of other people's animals.

13
00:01:18.319 --> 00:01:19.980
Kaleem was going to help her.

14
00:01:25.242 --> 00:01:26.743
paint a fish tank on this sign."

15
00:01:27.303 --> 00:01:29.084
Kaleem reached for the blue paint.

16
00:01:29.888 --> 00:01:32.789
He'd painted a cat and dog on some other signs.

17
00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:37.570
Daisy said.

18
00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.711
"Can you paint a parrot too?

19
00:01:40.591 --> 00:01:43.932
I want people to know we can take care of all kinds of animals."

20
00:01:43.952 --> 00:01:47.913
"Of course I can paint a parrot," Kaleem said.

21
00:01:47.933 --> 00:01:51.995
"I can paint any—aah!"

22
00:01:53.015 --> 00:01:55.956
Kaleem dropped his paintbrush and jumped to his feet.

23
00:01:58.828 --> 00:02:00.649
He waved his arms wildly.

24
00:02:00.669 --> 00:02:02.549
"What's wrong?"

25
00:02:02.829 --> 00:02:03.609
Daisy asked.

26
00:02:03.629 --> 00:02:05.470
"There's a bee!"

27
00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.631
Kaleem looked terrified.

28
00:02:07.651 --> 00:02:10.631
"I forgot to bring my EpiPen outside.

29
00:02:11.151 --> 00:02:12.352
I can't get stung!"

30
00:02:13.412 --> 00:02:16.573
Now Daisy understood why her friend was so upset.

31
00:02:17.673 --> 00:02:19.894
Kaleem was allergic to bee stings.

32
00:02:20.854 --> 00:02:24.955
And he didn't have his EpiPen–a medical device to protect him if he got stung.

33
00:02:24.975 --> 00:02:27.056
"There it is!"

34
00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.182
Kaleem swatted at something in the air.

35
00:02:30.202 --> 00:02:31.443
"Got it!"

36
00:02:32.484 --> 00:02:33.945
The bee fell to the ground.

37
00:02:33.965 --> 00:02:35.646
"Don't hurt it!"

38
00:02:37.568 --> 00:02:38.969
Daisy rushed closer.

39
00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:42.072
"There's a nicer way to shoo it away."

40
00:02:42.092 --> 00:02:44.154
"Maybe for you!"

41
00:02:44.174 --> 00:02:48.077
Kaleem laughed nervously.

42
00:02:48.097 --> 00:02:50.819
"Every animal we see loves you.

43
00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:52.481
But bees are pests.

44
00:02:53.301 --> 00:02:56.124
And if that one stings me, I could end up in the hospital!"

45
00:02:57.196 --> 00:02:58.597
"Bees aren't pests."

46
00:02:59.798 --> 00:03:02.641
Daisy bent down to look for the fallen insect.

47
00:03:02.661 --> 00:03:05.643
"They're an important part of our ecosystem.

48
00:03:06.184 --> 00:03:08.005
They help pollinate the food we eat.

49
00:03:08.946 --> 00:03:11.789
Bumblebees like that one are native to the United States.

50
00:03:12.809 --> 00:03:14.231
Some types are endangered!"

51
00:03:14.251 --> 00:03:16.553
"Thanks for the lecture, Professor."

52
00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:18.494
Kaleem rolled his eyes.

53
00:03:18.514 --> 00:03:21.637
"But I'll be endangered if that bee stings me!"

54
00:03:22.878 --> 00:03:24.840
Daisy finally located the bee.

55
00:03:25.896 --> 00:03:27.917
It was clinging to a blade of grass.

56
00:03:29.178 --> 00:03:30.599
Luckily it looked okay.

57
00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.821
Daisy gently picked it up.

58
00:03:33.841 --> 00:03:37.283
"Sorry about that, little bee," Daisy said.

59
00:03:37.303 --> 00:03:40.905
"Please leave my friend Kaleem alone, okay?

60
00:03:41.525 --> 00:03:43.086
He's allergic to your sting."

61
00:03:44.247 --> 00:03:46.188
The bee buzzed up into the air.

62
00:03:46.208 --> 00:03:49.470
"I'm not here for Kaleem.

63
00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:51.971
I'm here for you!"

64
00:03:52.492 --> 00:03:52.952
she said.

65
00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:57.125
But all Daisy and Kaleem heard was loud buzzing.

66
00:03:57.145 --> 00:03:59.486
"The bee sounds kind of mad."

67
00:04:00.266 --> 00:04:01.926
Kaleem looked nervous again.

68
00:04:01.946 --> 00:04:05.287
"I'd better go inside until it buzzes away."

69
00:04:05.307 --> 00:04:08.828
"Get your EpiPen while you're there," Daisy said.

70
00:04:10.989 --> 00:04:13.970
Kaleem ran off, and Daisy went back to painting.

71
00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.591
Suddenly she heard the bee buzzing closer.

72
00:04:19.631 --> 00:04:22.192
Then she felt it land on the back of her neck.

73
00:04:26.412 --> 00:04:27.754
"Ouch!" she cried.

74
00:04:27.775 --> 00:04:30.419
"Hey, you stung me!"
